2. Font metrics for the 14 PDF core fonts

Source: the Adobe Font Metrics (AFM) files of Courier, Helvetica, Times,
Symbol and ITC Zapf Dingbats, as published by Adobe.
Used for: internal/charset/corewidths_gen.go (glyph widths) and the
built-in encodings of Symbol and ZapfDingbats in
internal/charset/encodings_gen.go.

Modification notice: this module does not contain the AFM files. It
contains tables derived from them: of each glyph, only its width, and of
each font, only its encoding, rearranged by character. Everything else
in the files (kerning pairs, bounding boxes, composite characters) is
left out.

